    "lecture_name": "with students, assignments, and submissions tables. It didn't know you've been following REST API pa",
    "content": "with students, assignments, and submissions tables. It didn't know you've been following REST API patterns for eight weeks. It didn't know what \"assignment submission\" even means in your specific cohort workflow.\nSo it did what any reasonable system would do when given no context: it guessed. And its guesses were generic, safe, and useless.\nThis is the GIGO principle—Garbage In, Garbage Out. AI tools aren't mind readers. They're amplifiers. If you feed them vague instructions with no context, they amplify vagueness. If you feed them precise context, they amplify precision.\nNow picture this instead: You open the same tool. But this time, you first write a half-page document:\nPurpose: Track which students have submitted assignments for",
