    "content": "= scales to thousands of users. You didn't need new skills. Just git push.\n\nPHASE 4: TROUBLESHOOTING & READINESS\nThe Big Three Deployment Errors (Everyone Hits These)\nError 1: Port Binding\n# Breaks on Render\nuvicorn.run(app, port=8000)\n\n# Works on Render\nport = int(os.getenv(\"PORT\", 8000))\nuvicorn.run(app, host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=port)\n\nError 2: Missing Dependencies\n# Check what's installed locally\npip freeze\n\n# Compare to requirements.txt\ncat requirements.txt\n\n# Missing package? Add it\necho \"python-multipart\" >> requirements.txt\ngit commit -am \"Add missing dependency\"\ngit push\n\nError 3: Environment Variable Typos Check Render dashboard → Environment → Variables. Compare letter-by-letter to your .env. One wrong character = broken app.\n\nReading Logs (The Debugging Skill That Matters)\nWhen deploy fails, click \"Logs\" in Render dashboard. Look for:\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'groq'\n→ Missing from requirements.txt\n\nsqlalchemy.exc.OperationalError: connection refused\n→ Wrong Supabase URL in env vars\n\nAddress already in use: 0.0.0.0:8000\n→ Hardcoded port, need $PORT\n\nPractice: Intentionally break something, read the logs, fix it.\nThis builds debugging muscle memory.\n\nReadiness Check: \"Who Can Ship This Weekend?\"\nBy now you should be able to:\n✅ Deploy a FastAPI + Supabase app from GitHub\n ✅ Configure environment variables on a platform\n ✅ Fix port binding errors\n ✅ Read logs to diagnose issues\n ✅ Push updates via git and see auto-redeploy\n ✅ Test live app and confirm it matches localhost behavior\nQuestion: Can you walk me through deploying your",
